  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $3a\\cdot (2b\\times (-c))=8.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a\\cdot (2b\\times (-c)) & =8 \\\\ 3\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =8 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
